1
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
You'll believe a man can fly.

2
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Superman is a science fiction, action, adventure
film directed by Richard Donner.

3
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Mild-mannered Clark Kent works as a reporter at the Daily
Planet alongside his crush, Lois Lane.

4
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Clark must summon his superhero alter-ego when the nefarious Lex
Luthor launches a plan to take over the world.

5
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Clark Kent / Superman, played by Christopher Reeve.

6
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Lois Lane, played by Margot Kidder.

7
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Lex Luthor, played by Gene Hackman.

8
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Jor-El, played by Marlon Brando.

9
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Otis, played by Ned Beatty.

10
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Perry White, played by Jackie Cooper.

11
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Superman (also marketed as Superman: The Movie) is a 1978 superhero film based on
the DC Comics character Superman, portrayed by Christopher Reeve.

12
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
It is the first of four installments in the Superman
film series starring Reeve as Superman.

13
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
The film was directed by Richard Donner and written by Mario Puzo,
David Newman, Leslie Newman, and Robert Benton.

14
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The film features an ensemble cast including Marlon Brando, Gene Hackman, Ned Beatty, Jackie Cooper, Glenn Ford, Trevor
Howard, Margot Kidder, Valerie Perrine, Maria Schell,  Terence Stamp, Phyllis Thaxter and Susannah York.

15
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It depicts the origin of Superman, including his infancy as Kal-El of Krypton, son of
Jor-El (Brando), and his youthful years in the rural town of Smallville.

16
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
Disguised as reporter Clark Kent, he adopts a mild-mannered disposition in Metropolis and develops a
romance with Lois Lane (Kidder) while battling the villainous Lex Luthor (Hackman).

17
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Ilya Salkind had the idea of a Superman film in 1973 and, after a difficult process with DC
Comics, the Salkinds bought the rights to the character the following year.

18
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
Several directors, most notably Guy Hamilton, and screenwriters were
associated with the project before Donner was hired to direct.

19
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
Tom Mankiewicz was drafted in to rewrite the script and
was given a creative consultant credit.

20
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
It was decided to film both Superman and its sequel Superman II (1980) simultaneously, with
principal photography beginning in March 1977 and ending in October 1978.

21
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
Tensions arose between Donner and the producers, and a decision was made to stop filming the
sequel, of which 75 percent had already been completed, and finish the first film.

22
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:42,000
The most expensive film made up to that point, with a budget of $55 million, Superman premiered at The Kennedy Center in Washington, DC,
on December 10, 1978, and was released in the United Kingdom on December 14, and in the United States on December 15.

23
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
The film was a critical and financial success; its worldwide box office earnings of
$300 million made it the second-highest-grossing release of the year.

24
01:55:12,000 --> 01:55:18,000
It received praise for Reeve's performance and John Williams's musical score.

25
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
The film was nominated for Best Film Editing, Best Music (Original Score) and Best Sound at the 51st
Academy Awards and received a Special Achievement Academy Award for Visual Effects.

26
02:04:48,000 --> 02:04:54,000
Groundbreaking in its use of special effects and science fiction/fantasy storytelling, the film's
legacy presaged the mainstream popularity of Hollywood's superhero film franchises.

27
02:09:36,000 --> 02:09:42,000
In 2017, Superman was selected for preservation by the
Library of Congress's National Film Registry.

28
02:14:24,000 --> 02:14:30,000
The film explores themes of galaxy, journalist, saving
the world, secret identity, crime fighter.

29
02:19:12,000 --> 02:19:18,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
